<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Maranhão</h1><p class="st-meta">1621 CE – 1751 CE · capital São Luís</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A separate Portuguese colony covering the Amazon and the north coast of Brazil, governed directly from Lisbon rather than from Salvador.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After expelling the French of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/equinoctial-france">Equinoctial France</a> in 1615 and founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belem">Belém</a> in 1616, Portugal created the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranhao">Maranhão</a> in 1621, separate from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-brazil">State of Brazil</a>. Its capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-luis">São Luís</a>, and it included Grão-Pará, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceara">Ceará</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a> basin, which were easier to reach by sea from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> than from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The colony depended on indigenous labour to collect forest products such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cacao">cacao</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cloves">cloves</a> and sarsaparilla. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-teixeira">Pedro Teixeira's</a> expedition up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a> in 1637 to 1639 extended Portuguese claims. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-luis">São Luís</a> from 1641 to 1644. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-vieira">António Vieira</a> campaigned against the enslavement of indigenous people. Settlers resented Jesuit control and a trading company's monopoly, which led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beckman-revolt">Beckman Revolt</a> in 1684.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1751 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marquis-of-pombal">Marquis of Pombal</a> reorganised the colony as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-grao-para-and-maranhao">State of Grão-Pará and Maranhão</a>, with its capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belem">Belém</a> and his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-xavier-de-mendonca-furtado">Francisco Xavier de Mendonça Furtado</a> as governor.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1621 CE – 1751 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South America</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.96%;width:2.59%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1621 CE – 1751 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>São Luís</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Manuel Beckman</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Portuguese, Nheengatu</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/brazil">Brazil</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>State of Maranhão and Grão-Pará, Estado do Maranhão</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1686&amp;focus=state-of-maranhao" aria-label="State of Maranhão on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3450 2272 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where State of Maranhão lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3770 2528L3944 2917M3770 2528L4773 1044M3770 2528L3653 2488"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3944 2917h0M4773 1044h0M3653 2488h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3770 2528h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3770 2528h0"/>